# Fable Mode (project default)

This repo uses [fable-mode v3](https://github.com/mrtooher/fable-mode) for agent workflow.

## Always on

Read and follow `.cursor/skills/execution-guardrails/SKILL.md` on **every** task (verify-before-flag, warning threshold, safe find-and-replace).

## When to use fable-mode

Use `.cursor/skills/fable-mode/SKILL.md` when a task:

- spans multiple files, sources, or sessions
- the user asks for thorough / systematic / "deep work" handling
- needs staged verification (docs validation, large refactors, multi-page rewrites)

Skip fable-mode for single-pass tasks with one obvious approach.

## Delegation (installed agents)

Project agents live in `.cursor/agents/`:

| Agent | Role |
|-------|------|
| `fable-orchestrator` | Stage map + delegate (no Write/Edit) |
| `fable-worker-sonnet` | Reasoning / code / synthesis stages |
| `fable-worker-haiku` | Bulk mechanical stages |
| `fable-verifier` | Cold re-check of deliverables |

For peak quality on large work, route through **fable-orchestrator** (see `fable-opus` skill). For balanced cost, use **fable-sonnet**. For cheap bulk passes, **fable-haiku**.

## Skills

- `.cursor/skills/fable-mode/` — default inline loop
- `.cursor/skills/fable-opus/` / `fable-sonnet/` / `fable-haiku/` — model-pinned variants
- `.cursor/skills/execution-guardrails/` — always-on rules
